# What the image build does NOT need from the repo.
#
# This file exists because deploy/allinone/Dockerfile copies `.env*` from the context root.
# A glob at the root makes BuildKit enumerate the whole context, and the enumeration failed
# on a .pytest_cache directory Windows had locked — so the build broke on a file nothing
# was ever going to copy. Excluding the noise fixes that and makes the context smaller.
#
# NOTE: `.env` is deliberately NOT ignored. It is gitignored, and it is meant to reach the
# image — see the COPY .env* block in deploy/allinone/Dockerfile for what that does and what
# it costs. Adding `.env` here would silently undo that, and the build would still succeed,
# so anyone tempted to add it should change the Dockerfile instead.

# Caches and build output
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/.pytest_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/node_modules/
**/dist/
**/build/
**/.vite/
**/*.egg-info/

# VCS and editor
.git/
.gitignore
**/.DS_Store
.vscode/
.idea/

# Local runtime state that must never be baked in
**/*.log
**/uploads/
**/data/uploads/
**/data/doc_rag_uploads/
**/.venv/
**/venv/

# Scratch and coverage output
**/htmlcov/
**/.coverage

# Markdown is NOT excluded, and must not be. svc-deepagents/skills/*/SKILL.md is read at
# runtime: select_skill() routes every chat question by matching it against those files'
# triggers, so a `*.md` line here would leave the orchestrator with no skills to route to
# and break the chat interface — while the build still succeeded and every health check
# still returned 200. The eight files are:
#   compliance · contract-performance · doc-rag · energy-intelligence
#   migration · query-builder · udr · wo-engine
